                <pb facs="0601" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg507"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Dec. 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 447.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose recent
                    correspondence concerning Anton Yablkowski, whose case was reported in the
                    legation’s Nos. 144, 151, 157, 161, and 179 of September 28, October 10, 16, and
                    28, and November 29, 1895, respectively.</p>
                <p>It appears that Yablkowski is now at liberty, and I have requested our consul at
                    Warsaw to endeavor to ascertain what has become of him, in order to, if
                    possible, close up the case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D. Peirce</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>





